Z||000025||Santa Cruzer||07-10-2001||09:04 PM||||Atari ,died in 1996 when  jack tramiel the owner of the atari corp,and the origonal owner of commodore decided to merge with JTS, a small company that manufactured hard drives for laptops,from poor managment and lack of sale's in the almighty jaguar, atari could not stand up to the like's of sega,sony and nintendo, by murging with JTS they owned all the right's to atari and it's name all development's for the jag "includeing the awsome virtual headset were canceld" in 1998 hasbro bought all the right's to atari off of JTS for 5million ,and now releasd all the right's to make games for any atari system and belive it or not jag games are still being made today,not to mention the amount of new lynx games out..but atari just isin't atari anymore!... it's hasbro! not the same is it? anyway that's a brief story of how atari corp ended, sad but true<P><BR>ps: jack tramiel was rated the 3rd boss from hell in 1995,being known for lashing out at employee's when thing's didn't go right,for all the commodore fans this is the man that made commodore! but after 1986 it was sold to amiga corp and any pc from there on was commodore amiga ,it's also interesting to know that amiga desighned the lynx!!!<P>that's enough,any more question's just ask!..<P>------------------<BR>red candy apple copper burgandy color,tan interior all options,american racing rims,Pioneer Cd Player,pioneer 120w speakers"in factory location",sony ****  amp,and workin' on a girl to go with the package <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierose_1986/dts.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierose_1986/dts.html</A>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/me!!!.jpg">    <P>[This message has been edited by Santa Cruzer (edited 07-10-2001).]<P>[This message has been edited by Santa Cruzer (edited 07-10-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Santa Cruzer (edited 07-10-2001).]||||reg||7
