Z||000034||kslish||07-11-2001||12:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by The Fieromaster:<BR><B>I have an Intelevision...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I recently purchased an Intellivision off of eBay since I still have like 50 cartridges from my original 1981 era system that burnt out years and years ago.  Those things blow the old Atari 2600 games out of the water.<P>I've got an Atari Jaguar gathering dust too, an old NES, a Sega Genisis (with the CD attachment), and a Playstation (just for Gran Turismo).  <P>As for "personal" computers, I could've died for a Commodore 64 when I was little (but i was also jealous of my cousin's TI99/4A). Then my dad finally got an Apple II Plus from the school district he taught at.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Ahh, the memories of LodeRunner and Castle Wolfenstein.  And the "text based" adventure games....<P>Ken S.<p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 07-11-2001).]||||reg||1
